# Line endings are a reproducibility problem in this repo, not a style one.
#
# taskset.jsonl was generated on Windows and carried CRLF; results.jsonl was
# generated on Linux and carried LF. Two artefacts of one experiment disagreed
# about line endings, which means the same code on two machines produced
# byte-different files. That makes a hash-based regression gate impossible and
# it silently breaks any "the task set rebuilds byte-identically" claim.
#
# Fixed in two places: the writers pass newline="" so Python does no platform
# translation, and git is told to leave these files alone rather than
# normalising them on checkout.

*.jsonl  text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
